  "answer": "Karen Smith (CFO) revised the Q2 budget by shifting funds to emerging market bonds, resulting in a new profit forecast of $9.378 million (a 3.5% increase). Emily Rogers (Operations Manager) requested urgent approval for an unplanned $50,000 IT security expenditure, which will impact the Q2 budget. Marcus Li (Director of Operations) proposed cost-saving initiatives (vendor renegotiation, energy reduction, supply chain streamlining) that could save up to $200,000 in Q2. Additionally, Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) noted that the upcoming Q2 audit will require accurate financial records, particularly those related to the recent budget revisions."
